  "user_request_original": "Design a 23-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 defect-cavity bandpass filter on fused silica substrate for 1550 nm LiDAR application. Layer sequence: alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 starting with Ta2O5, with central Ta2O5 layer as half-wave cavity. Initialize all 23 layer thicknesses with strictly monotonic linear chirp from 150.0 nm (layer 1) to 300.0 nm (layer 23). Apply hard penalty constraint during optimization: maximum adjacent-layer thickness difference ≤15.0 nm. Optimize all 23 thicknesses to maximize transmittance at 1550 nm while minimizing transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands. Use gradient_thickness optimizer with thickness bounds 50-400 nm for all layers except cavity (300-700 nm). Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 5 alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 pairs, one cavity layer, and exactly 5 reverse-order pairs (21 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize 21 finite Ta2O5/SiO2 layers on fused silica to form a 1550 nm bandpass filter. Start with Ta2O5, alternate 5 pairs, insert a half-wave Ta2O5 cavity, then 5 reverse pairs. Initialize thicknesses via linear chirp 150–300 nm, constrain non-cavity layers to 50–400 nm and cavity to 300–700 nm. Maximize T at 1550 nm while minimizing T in 1400–1500 nm and 1600–1700 nm. Enforce maximum adjacent-layer thickness change of 15 nm.",
